A file stores 120,000 fixed-length records of an `ORDERS` relation in no particular order. A **dense secondary index** on the unique attribute `order_no` is built as a multilevel index:

- the first level has one entry (search key, record pointer) for every record;
- every higher level has one entry (search key, block pointer) for every block of the level immediately below it;
- levels are added until the topmost level fits in a single block.

The disk block size is $1024$ bytes, a search key takes $12$ bytes, and both a record pointer and a block pointer take $8$ bytes. Index entries are not spanned across blocks, and every index block, except possibly the last block of a level, is filled with as many entries as it can hold.

The total number of blocks occupied by the index, over all its levels, is ________.

